From: 78andyp <drandypowell@live.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:05:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [VideoInfoScanner] Resolve an episode's bluray playlist as an
 episode.

The media type of an episode was only set once it was added, after its
playlist had been resolved. With a scraper that doesn't give the media
type, the episode was resolved as a movie, i.e. to the disc's main
title, and without the duration and title that narrow the candidates.
---
 xbmc/video/VideoInfoScanner.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/video/VideoInfoScanner.cpp b/xbmc/video/VideoInfoScanner.cpp
index b9940dc..73c6b77 100644
--- a/xbmc/video/VideoInfoScanner.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/video/VideoInfoScanner.cpp
@@ -2674,6 +2674,8 @@ CVideoInfoScanner::~CVideoInfoScanner()
 
         // Determine bluray playlist(s) (if possible)
         // Also populates streamdetails if playlist(s) found
+        // Resolved as an episode whether or not the scraper gave the media type
+        scraperItem.GetVideoInfoTag()->m_type = MediaTypeEpisode;
         CFileItemList blurayItems;
         ResolveBlurayPlaylist(&scraperItem, blurayItems);
 
